outputs.L1:
A method and a geotextile protective tube mat for establishing a protective sealing layer in a landfill basin for industrial and mining slurries, wherein the landfill basin comprises at least a bottom area and an embankment ring, both of which are covered, at least up to the maximum filling level, with a single-ply or multi-ply base sealing layer. The method comprises the following steps:

- providing and using bottom protective tube mats (10) composed of a water-permeable, multi-ply geotextile fabric, in which at least a lower ply (17) and an upper ply (18) are directly connected to one another along a plurality of parallel connecting lines (11; 15), thereby forming, between adjacent connecting lines (11; 15), mutually separate flexible tubes (12), each having at least one filling opening (13);
- laying out the bottom protective tube mats (10) over the bottom area of the landfill basin;
- laying out embankment protective tube mats (10) over the embankment ring, with the flexible tubes (12) aligned in the direction of the embankment slope or at an acute angle thereto; and
- individually filling each flexible tube (12) with an aqueous suspension and sealing the filling openings (13).

outputs.L2:
A process and a geotextile protective tubular mat are provided for constructing a protective sealing layer in a landfill basin intended for industrial and mining slurries. The basin includes at least a floor region and a surrounding embankment, both of which are lined, at least to the maximum permitted fill height, with a base sealing layer formed from one or more plies.

The process comprises:

- providing and employing floor-protection tubular mats (10) made from a water-permeable, multilayer geotextile fabric, in which at least one lower layer (17) and one upper layer (18) are joined directly together along multiple parallel connection lines (11; 15);
- forming separate flexible tubes (12) between adjacent connection lines (11; 15), each tube having at least one filling aperture (13);
- positioning the floor-protection tubular mats (10) across the floor region of the landfill basin;
- arranging embankment-protection tubular mats (10) over the surrounding embankment so that the flexible tubes (12) extend either in the direction of the embankment slope or at an acute angle relative to that direction; and
- separately filling every flexible tube (12) with an aqueous suspension and subsequently closing the filling apertures (13).

counterfactuals.output:
The invention is a protective lining system for slurry landfill basins, settling ponds, or similar containment structures. It uses a **water-permeable, multi-ply geotextile mat** laid over the basin’s bottom and embankment sealing layers.

The mat consists of at least two connected geotextile sheets that form a series of elongated, flexible tubular chambers. Each tube has its own filling opening and can be filled independently—typically with sand, gravel, mortar, or another pumpable ballast material. Once filled, the tubes create a heavy, conformable protective layer that:

- holds the underlying sealing membrane in place;
- prevents damage from deposited slurry, equipment, erosion, and wave action;
- adapts to uneven or sloping basin surfaces;
- allows water to pass through the geotextile instead of building up hydrostatic pressure; and
- permits damaged or underfilled sections to be repaired or refilled individually.

The mats may be anchored, overlapped, or joined to cover both the basin floor and inclined embankments, producing a stable, permeable armor layer without requiring a rigid concrete covering.
